      tokenUtility: "Bitcoin primarily functions as a store of value and a medium of exchange, often referred to as \'digital gold.\' Ethereum\'s native token, Ether (ETH), is used to pay for transaction fees (gas) on the network and as a collateral for DeFi applications. It also plays a crucial role in securing the network through staking in the Proof-of-Stake consensus mechanism.",
      tokenomics: "Bitcoin has a hard cap of 21 million coins, with a deflationary issuance schedule (halving events). Ethereum\'s tokenomics have evolved with the shift to Proof-of-Stake and the implementation of EIP-1559, which burns a portion of transaction fees, potentially making ETH deflationary under certain network conditions. There is no hard cap on ETH supply, but issuance is controlled.",
