      bearCase: "Increased regulatory crackdowns on privacy tools could stifle innovation and fragment the market, leading to reduced liquidity and utility for certain assets. A poorly managed transition to quantum-resistant cryptography for Bitcoin could introduce instability. Persistent and sophisticated hardware wallet attacks erode investor confidence, leading to a flight from self-custody and potentially impacting overall market cap.",
      neutralCase: "The crypto market will likely continue its trajectory of innovation tempered by regulatory pressures and security challenges. Advancements in privacy, quantum-resistant tech, and hardware security will occur, but not without friction. Regulatory bodies will intensify oversight, leading to a more compliant but potentially less \'free\' crypto environment. Market participants will adapt, but volatility related to these developments will remain a constant factor.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A \'Neutral-to-Cautiously Bullish\' outlook. While significant regulatory and security hurdles exist, the industry\'s capacity for innovation and adaptation is high. The quantum threat is distant, allowing time for mitigation. Privacy solutions will face headwinds but may find niches. Hardware wallet security will improve through iterative enhancements and user education. The probability of catastrophic failure from any single issue remains low due to distributed development and market resilience, but localized impacts are likely.",
